WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.080
We've talked before about how during the Obama
Administration, Republican's insisted in baseless

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:12.299
conspiracy theories relating to President
Obama about Obama planning to, or wanting

00:00:12.299 --> 00:00:16.480
to, or scheming to stay in power longer than
two presidential terms.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:22.259
Sometimes it would be Obama's going to declare
martial law to justify suspending the 2016

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:23.259
election.

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:28.880
Sometimes it was Obama's going to change the
constitution so that presidents can have three

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.770
terms or unlimited terms or whatever.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:38.130
And anyone who had a good head on their shoulders
realized that from day one, it was absolutely

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.160
ridiculous and completely not based in fact.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.550
But there were lots of Republicans that fell
for that conspiracy just like they fell for

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.040
the Trump fomented birther conspiracy theory.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.320
So this unfortunately was a topic of discussion
among certain enclaves of the right while

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.550
Barack Obama was president.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.780
Obama will not relinquish power.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.360
He will do everything under the, under the
sun possible, uh, to try to stay in power

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.360
beyond 2016.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.000
Of course, it never happened and that was
completely predictable.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.580
Donald Trump, on the other hand, has actually
signaled that he at least has aspirations

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.170
to more than two presidential terms.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.780
And Donald Trump also has serious authoritarian
tendencies.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.580
And I'm not going to rehash the full list
of examples here, but lately Donald Trump

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.190
keeps quote joking about serving more than
two presidential terms.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.799
And to be clear, I've set up before, I don't
think Donald Trump would get away with it

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:35.720
if he tried, but Donald Trump continues to
reference this idea of staying in power for

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.190
more than eight years and over the weekend,
Trump sort of again alluded to this on Twitter,

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.630
take a look saying quote apolo should be done
on, which is the more dishonest and deceitful

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:51.130
newspaper, the failing New York Times or the
Amazon lobbyists, Washington Post.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.900
They are both a disgrace to our country, the
enemy of the people, but I just can't seem

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.040
to figure out which is worse.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:03.600
The good news is that at the end of six years
after America has been made great again and

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.729
I leave the beautiful White House.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:10.799
Do you think the people would demand that
I stay longer, keep America great?

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:15.459
Both of these horrible papers, we'll click
quickly, go out of business and be forever

00:02:15.459 --> 00:02:16.459
gone.

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:18.499
So by itself, this is like nothing.

00:02:18.499 --> 00:02:23.879
It's just another dumb tweet from the president,
sort of alluding to staying longer than eight

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:25.669
years in the White House.

00:02:25.669 --> 00:02:27.239
But remember the context.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:30.310
Remember what Donald Trump said before the
2016 election.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.890
He said he might not accept the results of
the 2016 election if they said that Hillary

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.150
Clinton had won.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.189
And by the way, he hasn't accepted the popular
vote results.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:41.529
He, yes, he did win electorally.

00:02:41.529 --> 00:02:46.620
He lost the popular vote badly by more than
any recent president has lost the popular

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.620
vote.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.859
And he doesn't accept that he has insisted
that three to 5 million people voted illegally

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:53.379
for Hillary Clinton.

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:58.959
Remember when Donald Trump said last year
behind closed doors to Republican donors that

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:03.379
he likes what the Chinese president has done
saying quote, he's now president for life

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:04.530
president for life.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.720
No, he's great.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.599
And look, he was able to do that.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:09.199
I think it's great.

00:03:09.199 --> 00:03:11.859
Maybe we'll have to give it a shot someday.

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:18.809
Once again, the tendency the appeal to Donald
Trump of the presidency, possibly for him

00:03:18.809 --> 00:03:21.049
lasting longer than eight years.

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:26.970
So as crystal is a row in a recent CNN op
Ed, I do not think that Donald Trump is going

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.030
to try to change the constitution to stay
in power, uh, beyond two terms.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:38.299
If he wins reelection, let's not do what Republicans
did under Barack Obama and go crazy with all

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:41.159
of these absurd conspiracy theories.

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:46.760
I do believe that Donald Trump is likely to
question the 2020 results if he loses and

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:51.010
to at least try to make the case that he was
not fairly defeated.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.739
And he's already started to lay the groundwork
for that.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:59.589
And I do expect Donald Trump to dance around
with the idea if he wins reelection in 2020

00:03:59.589 --> 00:04:04.069
that maybe he should remain in power beyond
that.

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:06.729
But I don't think that it's going to succeed
and I don't think that there's going to be

00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:11.849
any serious a case that Trump makes that would
actually challenge the sort of framework which

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:13.349
limits presidents to eight years.

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:14.349
Trump, yes.

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:15.349
Is a major authoritarian.

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:16.540
Trump, yes.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.850
Must get what he wants.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:24.980
Yes, Trump is the epitome of the sort of entitled
Rich Kid, but is he going to actually try

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.020
to forcefully stay in power?

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:32.120
I believe the answer is no and even if he
does there is no way that he could pull it

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.600
off even if he actually tries to do that.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:40.290
The point is if you were one of the people
before 2016 saying that Barack Obama is going

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:44.920
to try to stay in power, how can you not be
saying the same thing about Donald Trump?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:51.000
Because Donald Trump has actually shown us
that behind the curtain he likes the idea

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.110
of more than eight years as president and
he is more than willing to question the validity

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:00.600
and trustworthiness of election results when
the results simply don't suit him as that

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.130
entitled Rich Kid that he has been his entire
life.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.410
All I'm saying is there's a double standard
there.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.780
I don't believe that this is a real risk that
Donald Trump is going to try to carry out.

